ing the Classic alumni magazine, attending alumni events, and encouraging smart Christian students to check out your alma mater. Alumni @ NWC Connect Classic magazine Shop NWC Compass Center for Career & Calling Meet our grads Update your information Events Calendar Raider Nation Celebration (Homecoming) Get involved Give to NWC Refer a student Distinguished alumni National Alumni Board Work at NWC Giving Mission Investment Giving to Northwestern is more than just making a donation. It’s an investment in Christian higher education and students who will make a difference in God’s world. Giving @ NWC Give now Credit card Support a cause Endowed gifts Raider Athletics Association Theatre Patrons Music Patrons Planned giving Beneficiary designations Charitable gift annuities Charitable lead trusts Charitable remainder trusts Endowed gifts Heritage Society Memorial gifts Real estate Wills and living trusts Resources Advancement staff Update your information About Faith and learning Since 1882, Northwestern has been delivering an excellent education within the context of community and a Christian worldview. About NWC Learn about NWC Academic excellence Community + belonging History + heritage Orange City, Iowa Quick facts Student consumer info Work for NWC Why NWC? Mission and values Our mission Christian identity statement Vision for Learning Vision for Diversity People Leadership President Greg Christy News + Events Information. Invitation. There’s always something going on at Northwestern. Stay current with Northwestern news. Come to campus for concerts, plays, art exhibits, Raider sports and more. News + events @ NWC News & media Press releases Videos Events Campus calendar Alumni events Athletic events Continuing education Music concerts Theatre productions Visual art exhibits Marketing & Communications NWC logos and photos MarCom and web staff MYNWC Your campus connection MyNWC is a Web-based system that allows you to access information about your financial aid, housing assignment, billing status, course schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Assistant Professor of Strategic Communication Northwestern College seeks applicants for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of assistant professor in our English and communications department to begin August 2027. Interested candidates who have already attained higher rank may also inquire. The successful candidate can expect to teach courses in communications with specific emphases in strategic communication and public relations. The teaching load for this position is 24 credit-hours per academic year, normally three to four courses per semester. Responsibilities include teaching introductory and intermediate courses in communication, along with advanced courses in public relations. Required Qualifications: Candidates should hold a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a communications field. Near-completion ABDs are also welcome to apply. The successful candidate will demonstrate a keen ability to connect with our vibrant undergraduate students, sustain an active research program, build connections with local practitioners, and contribute to the life of the institution through faculty committees and other co-curricular service. Preferred Qualifications: While the primary focus of this position is strategic communication, strongest consideration will be given to those who also have additional experience in public relations. Our Department: Northwestern’s English and communications department celebrates professional and multimodal communication alongside literary study and theoretical practice. As the home for our journalism minor, our student newspaper ( The Beacon ), and our multimedia literary arts magazine ( The Archive ), our department promotes how storytelling flourishes in a variety of contexts and media platforms. Our current majors include public relations , writing and digital media , and English teaching . Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our calling to be a Christian academic community. Apply online below and send a current CV and a letter of interest to [email protected] . In your letter, (1) summarize your teaching experience; (2) describe your scholarly trajectory; and (3) discuss how our Christian Identity Statement would inform and shape your teaching and scholarship. Review of applications will begin on Oct. 15 and will continue until the position is filled. Apply online To apply for this position, use the button below to start or resume your application. Apply now Explore Application process Application instructions Employment application Contact us FAQs Benefits Faculty Staff Handbooks Faculty Employee Resources Living in Orange City Insurance MRF Clery Annual Security Report Home About Work at NWC Current openings APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
    },
