g the Classic alumni magazine, attending alumni events, and encouraging smart Christian students to check out your alma mater. Alumni @ NWC Connect Classic magazine Shop NWC Compass Center for Career & Calling Meet our grads Update your information Events Calendar Raider Nation Celebration (Homecoming) Get involved Give to NWC Refer a student Distinguished alumni National Alumni Board Work at NWC Giving Mission Investment Giving to Northwestern is more than just making a donation. It’s an investment in Christian higher education and students who will make a difference in God’s world. Giving @ NWC Give now Credit card Support a cause Endowed gifts Raider Athletics Association Theatre Patrons Music Patrons Planned giving Beneficiary designations Charitable gift annuities Charitable lead trusts Charitable remainder trusts Endowed gifts Heritage Society Memorial gifts Real estate Wills and living trusts Resources Advancement staff Update your information About Faith and learning Since 1882, Northwestern has been delivering an excellent education within the context of community and a Christian worldview. About NWC Learn about NWC Academic excellence Community + belonging History + heritage Orange City, Iowa Quick facts Student consumer info Work for NWC Why NWC? Mission and values Our mission Christian identity statement Vision for Learning Vision for Diversity People Leadership President Greg Christy News + Events Information. Invitation. There’s always something going on at Northwestern. Stay current with Northwestern news. Come to campus for concerts, plays, art exhibits, Raider sports and more. News + events @ NWC News & media Press releases Videos Events Campus calendar Alumni events Athletic events Continuing education Music concerts Theatre productions Visual art exhibits Marketing & Communications NWC logos and photos MarCom and web staff MYNWC Your campus connection MyNWC is a Web-based system that allows you to access information about your financial aid, housing assignment, billing status, course schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Business Faculty Northwestern College invites applications for a full-time business faculty position beginning in August 2027. The teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year. In addition to classroom instruction, the successful candidate will engage in scholarly activity and institutional service, including advising students, supervising program activities, and recruiting for the business and economics programs. We are seeking a versatile educator who can seamlessly bridge specialized agricultural courses with high-demand business offerings. Roughly half of the teaching load will focus on the agricultural business curriculum—delivering foundational and advanced courses such as Introduction to Ag Business, Ag Technology Systems, Ag Issues and Ethics, and Ag Risk and Cost Management, alongside overseeing student internships, practicums and advising the student Ag Club. The remaining portion of the load will support our core business program by teaching essential courses like Business Writing, Principles of Marketing, Consumer Behavior, Integrated Marketing Communication, and Small Business Management, with opportunities to introduce electives aligned with your specific scholarly or professional expertise. Required Qualifications: Applicants must hold at least a master’s degree in agricultural business, agricultural education, business administration or a closely related field, with candidates holding a master’s degree and significant professional experience considered for an instructor or professor of practice role. We seek faculty members who are committed to excellence in teaching, active scholarly engagement and the mission of the liberal arts as a vital expression of Christ's redemptive work in the world. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates holding an earned Ph.D. or terminal degree in agricultural business, business administration or a closely related field for a tenure-track appointment (ABD candidates considered). Ideal candidates will demonstrate excellence in undergraduate teaching, maintain research that engages students and show a strong commitment to relationship-centered mentorship. We seek a collaborative colleague who will enrich our departmental culture through service, shared purpose and a dedication to helping students flourish academically, professionally and personally. Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our mission. Apply online below and send a current CV and a letter of interest to vpaa@nwciowa.edu . In your letter, please (1) summarize your teaching experience, (2) describe your scholarly trajectory, and (3) discuss how our Christian Identity Statement would inform and shape your teaching and scholarship. Incomplete applications won’t be considered. Application deadline is November 15, 2026 . Apply online To apply for this position, use the button below to start or resume your application. Apply now Explore Application process Application instructions Employment application Contact us FAQs Benefits Faculty Staff Handbooks Faculty Employee Resources Living in Orange City Insurance MRF Clery Annual Security Report Home About Work at NWC Current openings APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
